  "final_files": {
    "numbers.py": "def total(values):\n    \"\"\"Return the sum of non-None values in *values*.\n\n    None values are ignored; zero and negative numbers are kept.\n    If the input is empty or contains only None values, return 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not values:\n        return 0\n    return sum(v for v in values if v is not None)\n",
    "labels.py": "def normalize(value):\n    \"\"\"Normalize a label by trimming outer whitespace and lowercasing.\n\n    Leading and trailing whitespace is removed, internal spaces are\n    preserved, and the remaining characters are converted to lowercase.\n    \"\"\"\n    if value is None:\n        return \"\"\n    return value.strip().lower()\n",
    "README.md": "# Helpers\n\nThis repository provides small utility functions.\n\n## `numbers.total(values)`\n\nComputes the sum of numeric values in an iterable while:\n\n- Ignoring any `None` values.\n- Keeping zero and negative numbers as-is.\n- Returning `0` when the input is empty or contains only `None`.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom numbers import total\n\ntotal([2, None, -1, 0])  # 1\ntotal([None])            # 0\ntotal([])                # 0\n```\n\n## `labels.normalize(value)`\n\nNormalizes a text label by:\n\n- Removing leading and trailing whitespace.\n- Preserving internal spaces.\n- Converting all remaining characters to lowercase.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom labels import normalize\n\nnormalize(\" A B \")   # \"a b\"\nnormalize(\"  \")      # \"\"\nnormalize(\"Name\")    # \"name\"\nnormalize(\"X  Y Z\")  # \"x  y z\"\n```\n",
    "test_numbers.py": "import unittest\nfrom numbers import total\n\nclass NumbersTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_total(self):\n        self.assertEqual(total([2, None, -1, 0]), 1)\n    def test_empty(self):\n        self.assertEqual(total([None]), 0)\n",
    "test_labels.py": "import unittest\nfrom labels import normalize\n\nclass LabelsTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_normalize(self):\n        self.assertEqual(normalize(' A B '), 'a b')\n    def test_empty(self):\n        self.assertEqual(normalize('  '), '')\n"
  },
